.TH DISKC 1 "September 2026" "diskc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diskc \- explain filesystem pressure, large files, growth, and writers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diskc
.RI [ path ...]
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B diskc light
.RI [ path ...]
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B diskc list
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B diskc db
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B diskc docker
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B diskc doc
.RI [ path ]
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B diskc mac system
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B diskc version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diskc
is a read-only disk troubleshooting command for Linux and macOS. It reports
filesystem and inode pressure, large allocated files and directories, observed
growth, active Linux writers, and deleted-but-open Linux files.
.PP
Without a path, diskc inspects the root filesystem. Multiple paths share one
growth-sampling window. Explicit paths are the opt-in mechanism for network
filesystems; automatic all-filesystem scans exclude remote mounts.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B light
Use a shallow scan, report ten entries, disable growth waiting, and skip process
file-descriptor inspection.
.TP
.B list
List mounted filesystems without traversing files. Remote and unknown mounts are
identified but are not probed, avoiding hangs on stale network mounts.
.TP
.B db
Discover common PostgreSQL, MySQL/MariaDB, Redis, ClickHouse, and MongoDB paths
and inspect their disk usage without connecting to a database.
.TP
.B docker
Inspect common Docker, containerd, BuildKit, and rootless storage locations
without requiring Docker daemon access.
.TP
.B doc
Show diskc's built-in defaults, build information, mount discovery, filesystem
access, capacity and inode pressure, and process inspection capability. The
default path is /; use an explicit path to check another filesystem. No file
tree is scanned. --json emits a machine-readable report.
.TP
.B mac system
Inspect common macOS system and user storage roots and provide conservative
cleanup guidance. Nothing is deleted.
.TP
.B version
Print version, commit, build date, Go version, and target platform.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --top " N"
Number of largest and fastest-growing files to report. Default: 20.
.TP
.BI --depth " N"
Maximum directory depth to scan. Default: 4.
.TP
.BI --sample " DURATION"
Growth measurement window. Default: 3s. Use 0 to disable.
.TP
.B --all
Inspect all automatically discovered local filesystems.
.TP
.B --watch
Refresh continuously. Terminal output is redrawn only when stdout is a terminal.
.TP
.BI --interval " DURATION"
Delay after each completed watch scan. Default: 3s.
.TP
.B --json
Emit JSON. With --watch, emit one compact JSON value per line (NDJSON).
.SH SIZE SEMANTICS
File and directory rankings use filesystem-allocated bytes rather than apparent
length. Sparse files therefore do not look like consumed disk space, and hard
links are counted once per scan. JSON also includes apparent bytes.
.PP
Filesystem output distinguishes used, free, available, reserved, and pressure.
Pressure is based on bytes unavailable to an unprivileged process.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success or help, 1 indicates a runtime failure, and 2 indicates
invalid command usage. Broken-pipe termination is treated as success.
.SH PERMISSIONS
No root access is required. Files and Linux process details hidden by permissions
cannot be reported; run diskc as the affected service user when practical.
.SH SAFETY
diskc is diagnostic and read-only. Validate findings before deleting files or
taking production action. See DISCLAIMER.md in the distribution.
.SH AUTHORS
diskc contributors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR df (1),
.BR du (1),
.BR lsof (8),
.BR find (1)
